    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d539">

                <pb facs="0617" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.01/58: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-03T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1919, 6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2182. For the Secretary of State and McCormick:</p>
                <p>Text of telegram from Semenoff to Admiral Kolchak submitted to Department by
                    Russian Embassy here. Semenoff recognizes Kolchak and submits unconditionally to
                    his command.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
